==Russian==

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{etyl|orv|ru}} {{term|азъбукы|tr=azъbuky|lang=orv}}, {{borrowing|cu|азъбоукꙑ|tr=azŭbuky|lang=orv}}, from the names of the first two letters of the Cyrillic alphabet, {{compound|азъ|боукꙑ|tr1=azъ|tr2=buky|lang=cu}}, a [[calque]] of {{etyl|grc|ru}} {{term|ἀλφάβητος||tr=alphabētos|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈazbʊkə/|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
'''азбука''' (ázbuka) {{f}}

# [[alphabet]]
#:* [[азбука Морзе]] — ''Morse code''
#:* [[азбука Брайля]] — ''Braille''
#:* [[слоговой|слоговая]] азбука — ''syllabary''
# ABC book, [[abecedary]]; [[primer]]
# [[ABC]] (''the rudiments of any subject'')

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-inan-vel-а-1|азбук|а́збук}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|alphabet}} [[алфавит]]
* {{sense|ABC book}} [[букварь]]
* {{sense|the rudiments of any subject}} [[основа|основы]], [[азы]]

[[Category:Russian nouns]]

