==Ukrainian==

===Etymology===
Created in {{etyl|orv|uk}} following {{term|азъбукы||tr=azъbuky|lang=orv}}, borrowed from {{etyl|cu|uk}} {{term|азъбоукꙑ|tr=azŭbuky|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}}, formed from the names of the first two letters in the [[Cyrillic alphabet]], {{term|азъ||tr=azŭ|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}} + {{term|боукꙑ|tr=buky|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}}, following the example of Greek {{term|ἀλφάβητος||lang=el|sc=Grek|tr=alphabētos}}.

Attested 1627, compare {{term||язъбука|tr=jazъbuka|lang=uk|sc=Cyrl}} (17–18th century).

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Uk-азбука.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{uk-noun|а́збука|f}}

# {{context|dated|lang=uk}} [[alphabet|Alphabet]] (an ordered set of letters used in a language), especially the old [[Cyrillic]] alphabet.

